guamp: guamp-gpu-all=1, a GPU connection for every process that opens the accelerator (NativeAdreno 81a0b01 + 0001..0004)

With native_adreno_gpu_all set by the board (GuampAdrenoProbe.cpp, boot-arg guamp-gpu-all=1; 0 = everything as before):
- 32 connection slots; the render server keeps slot 0 and its 1 GiB, every other connection gets a window sized on demand
  (192 MiB, else the largest free run of at least 64 MiB) from [0x60000000, end of the aperture), NativeAdrenoGpuAll.h;
- a teardown that clientClose cannot finish in 20 ms (jobs of a killed process still on the GPU) is retried by a kernel thread
  until it finishes; slot and window are reused only then (before, clientClose ran once and a failure kept them for the boot);
- limits: opens per name per minute (6) instead of 8 per boot, live connections (16, 2 per process), BO bytes per process (384 MiB)
  and of all of them (1024 MiB), a quarter of the shared GPU table kept for the render server; display hand-off and scanout stay
  the render server's; refused connections are detached from the registry.

